version: '1.0'
verdict: generation_bug
root_cause:
  category: coverage
  summary: The generated TB's coverage.py write() calls the non-existent .sample()
    method on the CoverPoint/CoverCross objects returned by coverage_db[...]. In the
    installed cocotb-coverage 1.2.0 these objects expose no .sample() method, so 10
    of 11 tests crash with AttributeError on the first monitor transaction before
    assertions and the scoreboard can complete. The library sampling mechanism is
    to call the decorator-wrapped functions, which the file already defines.
  evidence: 'All 11 tests report runtime_error (returncode 2, clean_exit=false). 10
    of 11 crash in AxiHandshakeCoverage.write at coverage.py:130 with AttributeError:
    ''CoverPoint'' object has no attribute ''sample'' (invoked from monitor.py:84
    via the pyuvm analysis port); RandomStimulusTest instead stops at assertions.py:116
    with the s_ready_only_when_can_accept violation (the intended detection of the
    deliberately-broken RTL). Verified by source inspection of cocotb-coverage 1.2.0
    and a standalone reproduction; _handshake_cross(...) and _payload_bins(...) sample
    successfully. simulation_result.json reports compatibility_findings: [].'
changes:
- file: coverage.py
  action: modify
  reason: coverage.py write() calls coverage_db['handshake_cg.input_transfer_bin'].sample(...),
    coverage_db['handshake_cg.output_transfer_bin'].sample(...), and coverage_db['payload_cg.payload_value_bin'].sample(...),
    but cocotb-coverage 1.2.0 CoverPoint/CoverCross expose no .sample() method, crashing
    every test on the first cycle in shared generated infrastructure.
  instructions:
  - Delete the two .sample() calls at lines 130-133 (coverage_db['handshake_cg.input_transfer_bin'].sample(input_transfer)
    and coverage_db['handshake_cg.output_transfer_bin'].sample(output_transfer)).
